  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "<div>The proposed development fails to respect the character and appearance of the original dwelling and the area.&nbsp; The introduction of a half-hipped roof extension would detract from the uniformity of the hipped roofscape in the surrounding context. The proposed roof would appear at odds within the local character and not sympathise with the existing roofscape in the surrounding area, especially at the prominent location where Cavendish Gardens and Sudbury Road joins, which would make the proposed roof seem abrupt from many nearby vantage points. As such, the proposed development is contrary to:<br></div><div><br></div><div><p><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">-\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework</span>&nbsp;(NPPF) (MHCLG, 2024);</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">- Policy D4 of the\r\nLondon Plan (March 2021);<o:p></o:p></span></p><p><span pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\" style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">- Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of t</span>he London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Local Plan (September 2024);</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 107%; font-family: \" pt=\"\" sans\",=\"\" sans-serif;\"=\"\">- The&nbsp;</span>London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 10.5pt;\">Residential\r\nExtensions and Alterations SPD (February 2012).</span></p></div>"
  ],
